AI USAGE STATEMENT
==================

The WHY2 ecosystem does not and will not contain any generative AI
features. By "AI" I mean LLMs/generative models specifically - not
machine learning in general (e.g. noise cancellation), which isn't
what this policy is about. This project was created on the basis of
my paranoid tendencies. Privacy always was the main focus of this
project and AI won't change that.
That being said, I actively use LLMs (mostly Claude) in WHY2
development. This file summarizes my personal AI policies.

First of all, any sensitive part of the codebase (REX, encryption,
authentication, etc.) won't get affected by AI. AI is most commonly
used in the chat frontend development, the part the end user (you,
hopefully) sees. I am absolutely terrible at creating something pretty
and no one volunteered to do it for me, so most of what you see is
generated by AI. Another feature of chat that was written using AI is
screensharing, specifically the screen capture and playback.

The REX documentation (rustdoc) is also mostly generated by AI, as
English isn't my first language.

Before using any AI code, I try to review it as much as possible. If
you have a problem with AI code being used in the application you use,
I completely understand it and have a solution for you - contribute to
the project.

Unless stated otherwise, assume all other "talkative" files in this
repo (README, SECURITY, etc.) may also be AI written. This file is the
one exception I'm explicitly confirming as fully human-written.
